{number: 109}
{title: Face to Face with Christ}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Face to face with Christ, my Savior,
Face to face—what will it [G7] be,
When with [C] rapture I be-[F] hold Him,
Jesus [C] Christ Who [G7] died for [C] me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Face to face I [G7] shall behold Him,
Far beyond the starry [C] sky;
Face to face in all His [F] glory,
I shall [C] see Him [G7] by and [C] by!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Only faintly now I see Him,
With the darkling veil be-[G7] tween,
But a [C] blessed day is [F] coming,
When His [C] glory [G7] shall be [C] seen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
What [C] rejoicing in His presence,
When are banished grief and [G7] pain;
When the [C] crooked ways are [F] straightened,
And the [C] dark things [G7] shall be [C] plain.
{end_of_verse}
